          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong nuclear object
            is a categorical generalization of the concept of a finite-dimensional vector space, or more generally, a finite-dimensional object.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_a_symmetric_monoidal_closed_category In a symmetric monoidal closed category
          %p
            A
            = succeed "in" do
              %em nuclear object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+closed+category"} symmetric monoidal closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            with unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that the canonical morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi _A:A\otimes A^*\to [ A, A]
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*:=[A,k]
            is an isomorphism.
          %p
            A
            %em morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            is called
            %em nuclear
            if there exists a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:k\to B\otimes A^*
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mo ⊗
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                          %mi ϕ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{k &amp; \overset{p}{\to} &amp; B\otimes A^*\\
                  n(f)\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow\phi\\
                  \&amp; [A,B] &amp; }
          %p
            is commutative, where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n(f)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\otimes A\simeq A\overset{f}{\to} B
          %h3#in_a_linearly_distributive_category In a linearly distributive category
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CockettSeely99"} CS’99
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linearly+distributive+categories"} linearly distributive categories
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is nuclear precisely if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_A
                is nuclear.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is nuclear then the canonical map to the double dual
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta _A: A\to A^{**}
                is an isomorphism.
            %li
              %p
                The full subcategory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi nuc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} nuc(\mathcal{M})
                of nuclear objects is symmetric monoidal closed.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is nuclear precisely if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^*
                is nuclear.
            %li
              %p
                In a cartesian monoidal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                only
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                is nuclear.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is nuclear there exists a natural
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
                morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mi A
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo *
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi A
                          %mo *
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_A:[A,A]\simeq A\otimes A^*\simeq A^*\otimes A \to k
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Nuclear objects in the category of complete semilattices are precisely the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+distributive+lattices"} completely distributive lattices
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
                %em constructively completely distributive lattices
                (Higgs&amp;Rowe 1989, Rosebrugh&amp;Wood 1994).
            %li
              %p
                Nuclear objects in the category of pointed sets are precisely the pointed sets with cardinality
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq 2
            %li
              %p
                Nuclear objects in the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
                with morphisms the bounded maps are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+spaces"} nuclear spaces
                (Rowe 1988).
